r, binds to the spindle microtubules and is involved in bipolar mitotic spindle assembly</article-title><source>J. Cell Sci.</source><volume>111</volume><year>1998</year><fpage>557</fpage><lpage>572</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9454730</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="Rojnuckarinetal1999"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Rojnuckarin</surname><given-names>P.</given-names></name><name><surname>Drachman</surname><given-names>J.G.</given-names></name><name><surname>Kaushansky</surname><given-names>K.</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Thrombopoietin-induced activation of the mitogen-activated protein kinase (MAPK) pathway in normal megakaryocytesrole in endomitosis</article-title><source>Blood.</source><volume>94</volume><year>1999</year><fpage>1273</fpage><lpage>1282</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10438715</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="Schumacheretal1998"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Schumacher</surname><given-names>J.M.</given-names></name><name><surname>Golden</surname><given-names>A.</given-names></name><name><surname>Donovan</surname><given-names>P.J.</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>AIR-2an Aurora/Ipl1-related protein kinase associated with chromosome and midbody microtubules is required for polar body extrusion and cytokinesis in <italic>Caenorhabditis elegans</italic> embryos</article-title><source>J. Cell Biol.</source><volume>143</volume><year>1998</year><fpage>1635</fpage><lpage>1646</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9852156</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="Sherr1995"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Sherr</surname><given-names>C.J.</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>D-type cyclins</article-title><source>Trends Biochem. Sci.</source><volume>20</volume><year>1995</year><fpage>187</fpage><lpage>190</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmi